# Triton's causal attention (tut_ll): the loop at tut_attn.py:140,
# `$L__BB0_42`, runs %ctaid.x trips, the CTA's row block, on the 128
# threads of the first four warps of CTAs with %ctaid.x >= 1. That
# condition decides which threads enter the loop, so over the record's
# 16x128 CTAs each CTA's threads count its trips, Σ x · 128 · 128 =
# 1,966,080 executions per instruction.
RUN: %ptxroof analyze %fixtures/b200/tut_ll_BM128_BN128_w4_s2_wsTrue.attn_fwd.sm_100a.ptx --ncu %fixtures/b200/tut_ll_BM128_BN128_w4_s2_wsTrue.attn_fwd.sm_100a.ncu.json | FileCheck --check-prefix=ANN "%s"
ANN: {{^}}$L__BB0_42:                             // %__nv_exp2f.exit535 // loop: trips %ctaid.x | warp 0-3 × lane * | CTAs 128·%ctaid.x ≥ 1 (1920/2048) | exec 1,966,080/launch{{$}}
